{"content":[{"c":["ASAPH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Berechiah’s son, an important tabernacle musician during King David’s reign (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.31-32,39","r":"1Chr.6.31-32,39","rawR":"1Chr.6.31-32,39","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.31-32,39","value":"1Chr.6.31-32,39"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 6:31-32, 39"},"). Along with Heman, the head singer, and Ethan, Asaph was appointed to sound bronze cymbals during the ceremony when the ark was brought to the new tabernacle (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.15.1-19","r":"1Chr.15.1-19","rawR":"1Chr.15.1-19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.15.1-19","value":"1Chr.15.1-19"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 15:1-19"},"). David appointed Asaph to serve “by giving constant praise and thanks to the Lord God of Israel” (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.16.4-5","r":"1Chr.16.4-5","rawR":"1Chr.16.4-5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.16.4-5","value":"1Chr.16.4-5"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 16:4-5"},", ",{"c":["tlb"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},") and to lead Israel in a special psalm of praise (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.16.7-36","r":"1Chr.16.7-36","rawR":"1Chr.16.7-36","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.16.7-36","value":"1Chr.16.7-36"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 16:7-36"},"). Along with his relatives he ministered daily before the ark (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.16.37","r":"1Chr.16.37","rawR":"1Chr.16.37","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.16.37","value":"1Chr.16.37"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 16:37"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.25.6,9","r":"1Chr.25.6,9","rawR":"1Chr.25.6,9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.25.6,9","value":"1Chr.25.6,9"}],"t":"ref","v":"25:6, 9"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Esd.1.15","r":"1Esd.1.15","rawR":"1Esd.1.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Esd.1.15","value":"1Esd.1.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Esd 1:15"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Esd.5.27,59","r":"1Esd.5.27,59","rawR":"1Esd.5.27,59","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Esd.5.27,59","value":"1Esd.5.27,59"}],"t":"ref","v":"5:27, 59"},"). He was also described as David’s private prophet (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.25.1-2","r":"1Chr.25.1-2","rawR":"1Chr.25.1-2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.25.1-2","value":"1Chr.25.1-2"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 25:1-2"},"). Asaph’s name appears in the superscriptions of ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.50.1-23","r":"Ps.50.1-23","rawR":"Ps.50.1-23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.50.1-23","value":"Ps.50.1-23"}],"t":"ref","v":"Psalms 50"}," and ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.73.1-83.18","r":"Ps.73.1-83.18","rawR":"Ps.73.1-83.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.73.1-83.18","value":"Ps.73.1-83.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"73–83"}," and in the guild he established, “the sons of Asaph” (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.25.1","r":"1Chr.25.1","rawR":"1Chr.25.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.25.1","value":"1Chr.25.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 25:1"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.35.15","r":"2Chr.35.15","rawR":"2Chr.35.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.35.15","value":"2Chr.35.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 35:15"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.2.41","r":"Ezra.2.41","rawR":"Ezra.2.41","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.2.41","value":"Ezra.2.41"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 2:41"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.7.44","r":"Neh.7.44","rawR":"Neh.7.44","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.7.44","value":"Neh.7.44"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 7:44"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.11.22","r":"Neh.11.22","rawR":"Neh.11.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.11.22","value":"Neh.11.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"11:22"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Joah’s father. Joah was the recorder (court historian or royal scribe) in King Hezekiah’s administration (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.18.18,27","r":"2Kgs.18.18,27","rawR":"2Kgs.18.18,27","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.18.18,27","value":"2Kgs.18.18,27"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 18:18, 27"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.36.22","r":"Isa.36.22","rawR":"Isa.36.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.36.22","value":"Isa.36.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 36:22"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Temple guard or gatekeeper, seemingly the same person as Ebiasaph (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.9.18","r":"1Chr.9.18","rawR":"1Chr.9.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.9.18","value":"1Chr.9.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 9:18"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["4. Keeper of the king’s forest in Palestine under Artaxerxes I Longimanus (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.2.8","r":"Neh.2.8","rawR":"Neh.2.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.2.8","value":"Neh.2.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 2:8"},"). Nehemiah asked this Asaph for timber to rebuild the wall, gates, and structures of Jerusalem."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Asaph","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Chr 6:31-32, 39","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.6.31-32,39","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.6.31-32,39","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.6.31-32,39"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 15:1-19","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.15.1-19","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.15.1-19","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.15.1-19"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 16:4-5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.16.4-5","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.16.4-5","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.16.4-5"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 16:7-36","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.16.7-36","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.16.7-36","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.16.7-36"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 16:37","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.16.37","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.16.37","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.16.37"},{"anchorText":"25:6, 9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.25.6,9","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.25.6,9","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.25.6,9"},{"anchorText":"1 Esd 1:15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Esd.1.15","rawQueryValue":"1Esd.1.15","sourceRefExact":"1Esd.1.15"},{"anchorText":"5:27, 59","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Esd.5.27,59","rawQueryValue":"1Esd.5.27,59","sourceRe